  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA encoders (scvi_n200 at 0.520, pca_n2000 at 0.485) dominate over image-only models (~0.21-0.23), and the best result so far (config_034, multimodal scvi_n200+ViT concat) is only marginally above RNA-only scvi_n200. The multiprofile dimension is completely untested across all 5 completed experiments, representing the largest source of uncertainty in the design space. Question: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly compares against config_004 (same RNA encoder, singleprofile) to isolate whether aggregating multiple profiles improves the dominant RNA signal, using the simplest aggregation (avgpool) as a conservative first probe. Why this is the best next experiment: Since RNA carries most of the predictive signal, establishing whether multiprofile helps at the RNA level before committing to more complex multimodal-multiprofile configurations (which confound profile-setting, aggregation, and fusion effects) is the most information-efficient use of the next budget slot. A positive result would justify investing in multimodal multiprofile variants (e.g., config_036/038); a null result would redirect effort toward fusion strategies or alternative encoders."
}

